# Build context hygiene. Two rules matter here beyond image size:
#
#   1. The family's documents must never enter an image. chroma_db/ and bm25_indexes/
#      are the only copy of them (ARCHITECTURE.md §5) and a layer is world-readable to
#      anyone who pulls the tag.
#   2. venv/ must never be copied in. It is ~2.1GB, it is built for the host's Python
#      and CPU, and startup.sh prefers ./venv over the image's interpreter if it exists
#      — so a stray copy would silently shadow the environment the Dockerfile built.
venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# User data (mirrors .gitignore — these live on the volume at runtime, never in a layer)
chroma_db/
bm25_indexes/
telemetry/
docs/raw/
docs/extracted/
*.pdf
*.pkl

# Eval outputs and local scratch.
#
# NOTE what is deliberately NOT here: evaluation/ itself. The harness scripts, eval.sh
# and the gold sets ship inside the GPU image on purpose — SETUP.md's GPU eval run
# invokes `bash evaluation/eval.sh` on the pod, and under the image-based deploy path
# (SETUP.md §0) there is no repo checkout there to fall back on. It is ~600KB against a
# multi-GB CUDA image, so excluding it would break a documented workflow to save
# nothing. results/ is excluded because it is 2.6MB of machine-specific run output that
# belongs to the box that produced it.
evaluation/results/
evaluation/goldset.raw.jsonl
evaluation/goldset_review.md

.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
